  <div class="root" id="rootSSR"><a href="#a11y-main" class="skip-link sr-text" data-cs="black">Jump to the content</a><a href="#a11y-footer" class="skip-link sr-text" data-cs="black">Jump to the footer</a><header id="a11y-siteheader" class="siteheader sh  "><div class="sh__inner ls-container ls-gutter"><div class="sh__nav "><a href="/en/visit" title="Go to homepage" class="rp-logo sh__logo"><span class="sr-text">Go to homepage</span><span class="rp-logo__pre sh__logopre">Visit</span><span class="rp-logo__text sh__logotext">Rotterdam</span></a><div class="sh__navwrap"></div><div class="sh__utilities"><a href="/en/visit/my-list" class="mylistlink link--small link link--secondary"><span class="sr-text">My List</span><svg class="mylistlink__icon" width="30" height="30" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg><span class="mylistlink__label">0</span></a><a href="/en/visit/rotterdam-city-card" title="Rotterdam City Card" class="promolink button button--primary">Rotterdam City Card</a><a href="/en/visit/search" class="searchlink link link--secondary link--small"><span class="sr-text">Search through our website</span><svg class="searchlink__icon" width="25" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--search"></use></svg></a><details id="ndl" class="navdrop navdrop--lang"><summary class="navdrop__toggler link link--secondary link--small"><svg class="navdrop__globe" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--globe"></use></svg><span class="link__label">en</span><svg class="navdrop__icon" width="6" height="12" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--chevron"></use></svg></summary><nav id="a11y-langnav" class="navdrop__inner" aria-label="Language"><ul class="navdrop__list"><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/nl/visit/guide/top-10-must-sees-voor-architectuurliefhebbers-in-rotterdam" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small "><span class="link__label">nl</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/visit/guide/top-10-architecture-rotterdam" aria-current="true" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small active"><span class="link__label">en</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/de/visit/guide/top-10-highlights-fuer-architekturbegeisterte-in-rotterdam" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small "><span class="link__label">de</span></a></li></ul></nav></details><button id="a11y-sitenav-toggler" class="sh__toggler" aria-controls="a11y-sitenav" aria-expanded="false"><span class="sr-text">Open the menu</span><span class="sh__togglericon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sh__togglerline"></span><span class="sh__togglerline"></span><span class="sh__togglerline"></span><span class="sh__togglerline"></span></span></button></div></div></div><div class="outernav sh__topnav"><nav id="a11y-topnav" class="outernav__inner sh__topnavinner ls-gutter" aria-label="Secondary"><ul class="outernav__list sh__topnavlist"><li class="sh__topnavitem"><details id="ndt" class="navdrop navdrop--top"><summary class="navdrop__toggler link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">All our services</span><svg class="navdrop__icon" width="6" height="12" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--chevron"></use></svg></summary><div class="navdrop__inner"><ul class="navdrop__list"><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/visit" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">Visit</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/conventions" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">Conventions</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/invest" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">Invest</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/trade" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">International Trade</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/internationals" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">Internationals</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/press" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">Press &amp; Media</span></a></li><li class="navdrop__item"><a href="/en/partners" class="navdrop__link link link--secondary link--small"><span class="link__label">Partners</span></a></li></ul></div></details></li></ul></nav></div></header><main lang="en" id="a11y-main" class="main main--cmsVisitPage "><div class="main__inner"><article class="page"><header class="
        pageheader ph
        ph--image
        ph--experience ph--outside
      " data-cs="beige"><div class="ph__titlewrap ls-spacing ls-gutter ls-grid"><h1 class="ph__title title--xxl ls-gutter--desk-s">Architecture Rotterdam: top 10 must-sees for architecture lovers</h1></div><div class="ph__inner ls-container ls-spacing ls-gutter"><div class="ph__wrap ls-container--m ls-spacing--desk ls-gutter--desk-s"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumbs"><div class="breadcrumbs__inner"><ol class="breadcrumbs__list text--xs"><li class="breadcrumbs__item ancestor"><a href="/en" class="breadcrumbs__link"><span class="breadcrumbs__label">Home</span></a></li><li class="breadcrumbs__item ancestor"><a href="/en/visit" class="breadcrumbs__link"><span class="breadcrumbs__label">Visit</span></a></li><li class="breadcrumbs__item parent"><a href="/en/visit/guide" class="breadcrumbs__link"><span class="breadcrumbs__label">Guide</span></a></li></ol></div></nav><div class="ph__text "><p class="ph__intro text--xxl">Rotterdam is known worldwide for its bold and innovative approach to architecture. After the Second World War, the city chose not to rebuild what was lost, but to look ahead. That decision shaped a skyline full of experiments, contrasts and new ideas. This list highlights ten places that show why architecture in Rotterdam continues to attract architects, designers and curious visitors from around the world.</p></div></div></div><div class="ph__visual ph__visual--outside" aria-hidden="true"><div class="fit-object"><img loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" class="ph__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1920px) 1800px, 100vw" alt="" width="1800" height="840" srcset="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Stadhuis_Rotterdam_Binnentuin_Garden_558_A6979_c02f79c4bf.webp 500w, https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/medium_Stadhuis_Rotterdam_Binnentuin_Garden_558_A6979_c02f79c4bf.webp 750w, https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/large_Stadhuis_Rotterdam_Binnentuin_Garden_558_A6979_c02f79c4bf.webp 1000w, https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/xlarge_Stadhuis_Rotterdam_Binnentuin_Garden_558_A6979_c02f79c4bf.webp 1920w" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Stadhuis_Rotterdam_Binnentuin_Garden_558_A6979_c02f79c4bf.webp"></div><div class="ph__actions"><button class="button button--primary button--bookmark "><svg class="button__icon " width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg><span class="button__label">loading</span></button></div></div></header><section id="textBlock-0" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="1-de-rotterdam" class="block__title title--l">1. De Rotterdam</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Designed by OMA and Rem Koolhaas, <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/de-rotterdam" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">De Rotterdam</a> is often described as a vertical city. Completed in 2013 on the Wilhelminapier, the building combines housing, offices and a hotel in three stacked towers. Its shifting volumes reflect the density and energy of the city. For a great view of the building itself, head to <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/gastrobar-elvy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elvy Gastro Bar</a> in the nhow hotel.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-1"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Watertaxi sailing the river Maas, with the Erasmus bridge and part of the Wilhelminapier skyline visible." width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Watertaxi_en_skyline_Iris_van_den_Broek_e7c698e35a.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">De Rotterdam</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-2" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="2-de-zalmhaven" class="block__title title--l">2. De Zalmhaven</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Finished in 2022, De Zalmhaven is the tallest residential building in the Netherlands. Designed by Dam &amp; Partners, the tower stands in the Scheepvaartkwartier and is accompanied by lower buildings that soften its presence in the neighbourhood. From <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/celest" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">restaurant Celest</a> on the 57th floor, you can take in wide views across Rotterdam.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-3"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Zalmhaven_Iris_van_den_Broek_023_A0515_2b58f2d473.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">De Zalmhaven</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-4" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="3-erasmus-bridge" class="block__title title--l">3. Erasmus Bridge</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Since 1996, <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/erasmusbrug" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Erasmus Bridge</a> has connected the city centre with Kop van Zuid. Designed by UNStudio, the bridge is easily recognised by its steel pylon, shaped like a swan’s neck. It is both a vital traffic connection and one of the most photographed icons of Rotterdam.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-5"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Een foto van de facade met ruiten van De Rotterdam met een weerspiegeling van de Erasmusbrug" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Skyline_De_Rotterdam_Robi_Utrecht_c43774c3cf.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Erasmusbrug</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-6" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="4-fenix" class="block__title title--l">4. Fenix</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Opened in 2025 on Katendrecht, <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/fenix" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fenix </a>is housed in a former harbour warehouse from 1923. The transformation includes the Tornado, a striking double spiral staircase designed by MAD Architects. The building brings together Rotterdam’s harbour past and its cultural present in one bold intervention.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-7"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="People enjoying the view of Rotterdam while visiting museum Fenix." width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Fenix_Iris_van_den_Boek_MG_4704_311a4bc953.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Fenix</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-8" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="5-cube-houses-kubuswoningen" class="block__title title--l">5. Cube Houses (Kubuswoningen)</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>The Cube Houses, designed by Piet Blom and completed in 1984, remain one of Rotterdam’s most playful architectural experiments. The tilted yellow cubes sit above a pedestrian area and challenge traditional ideas of living space. A visit to the <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/kubuswoningen-kijk-kubus-museumwoning" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kijk-Kubus</a> offers insight into how these homes are laid out.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section id="featuredListBlock-9" class="block block--featured-content"><div class="block--slider clickables-offset" data-cs="color yellow"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><header class="block__header--indented ls-gutter--desk-s"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 class="block__title title--l">Save at least 25% on these architectural highlights and more than 50 museums, tours and restaurants</h2><div class="rcc-badge"><a href="/en/visit/rotterdam-city-card" class="rcc-badge__link" title="Read more about the Rotterdam City Card"><img class="rcc-badge__logo" loading="lazy" width="155" height="40" alt="Rotterdam City Card" src="/images/spa/logo-rcc-hor.svg" srcset="" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></a></div></div></header><div class="block__content"><ul class="grid" style="--slider-offset: 0;"><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/finder-locations/kubuswoningen-kijk-kubus-museumwoning" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="/cdn-image/width=1200,quality=85,format=webp/https%3A%2F%2Fapp.thefeedfactory.nl%2Fapi%2Fassets%2F5ff8a152de7e8633a4ab7b2b%2Ff9c6eae8-fbb1-41fe-b548-e1d46afd7f35.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Kijk-Kubus museum house</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 148px;">The Cube Houses are one of the highlights of Rotterdam. The remarkable yellow houses on pylons are attracting many visitors. The Kijk-Kubus museum house gives an impression of how it is to live inside.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.15s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/finder-locations/nieuwe-instituut" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="/cdn-image/width=1200,quality=85,format=webp/https%3A%2F%2Fapp.thefeedfactory.nl%2Fapi%2Fassets%2F6639da37846e6a642361a06d%2FGevel_Nieuwe_Instituut1.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Nieuwe Instituut</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 148px;">Nieuwe Instituut is the national museum for architecture, design and digital culture. They have changing exhibitions on show and weekly different events, such as book presentations and research nights.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.3s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/finder-locations/huis-sonneveld" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="/cdn-image/width=1200,quality=85,format=webp/https%3A%2F%2Fapp.thefeedfactory.nl%2Fapi%2Fassets%2F5ff8a042de7e8633a4ab77a3%2Fcf7a3f61-923b-4a47-8b3e-ee525dbfe298.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Sonneveld House</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 204px;">Sonneveld House is one of the best-preserved residences in the New Building style. The villa on the edge of the Museum Park in Rotterdam was designed by the architectural firm Brinkman and Van der Vlugt, known for the Van Nelle Factory, among others. Visitors discover how a wealthy Rotterdam family lived in the 1930s.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.44999999999999996s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/finder-locations/stadion-feyenoord-de-kuip" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="/cdn-image/width=1200,quality=85,format=webp/https%3A%2F%2Fapp.thefeedfactory.nl%2Fapi%2Fassets%2F6564c5ce7a667b4df3775308%2Ftb220202TOM04582.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Stadium Tour De Kuip</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 120px;">De Kuip, as Stadion Feijenoord is popularly known, has been the home of Rotterdam football club Feyenoord since 1937. Visitors can also go there for tours, the museum and concerts.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.6s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/finder-locations/kunsthal-rotterdam" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="/cdn-image/width=1200,quality=85,format=webp/https%3A%2F%2Fapp.thefeedfactory.nl%2Fapi%2Fassets%2F68ee4bb1e23f496d04d9a60f%2F1920-Persbeeld_Kunsthal_Rotterdam_westzijde_foto_Jeroen_Musch.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Kunsthal Rotterdam</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 148px;">Kunsthal Rotterdam is known for its dynamic and surprising programme, suitable for a wide audience. From design to fashion, photography and paintings: that and more is covered in the exhibitions.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li></ul><div class="gridnav"><button class="gridnav__button gridnav__prev" disabled=""><div class="gridnav__buttoninner"><span class="sr-text">Previous</span><svg class="gridnav__icon" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--arrow-thin"></use></svg></div></button><button class="gridnav__button gridnav__next"><div class="gridnav__buttoninner"><span class="sr-text">Next</span><svg class="gridnav__icon" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--arrow-thin"></use></svg></div></button></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-10"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Een foto van de Kubuswoningen met op de achterzijde het Witte Huis in de Oude Haven" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Kubuswoningen_het_Witte_Huis_Iris_van_den_Broek_ac3ac0c1e2.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Kubuswoningen</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-11" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="6-kunsthal-rotterdam" class="block__title title--l">6. Kunsthal Rotterdam</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Located in Museumpark, the <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/kunsthal-rotterdam" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kunsthal </a>opened in 1992 and was designed by Rem Koolhaas and OMA. The building is known for its unusual routing and mix of materials, including concrete, glass and steel. There is no fixed visitor route, making the architecture itself part of the experience.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-12"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Exterior view of Kunsthal Rotterdam, a modern museum building with large windows and an orange sign, surrounded by trees and people walking on the plaza in front." width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Kunsthal_Rotterdam_westzijde_foto_Jeroen_Musch_d79ee351cb.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Kunsthal Rotterdam</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-13" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="7-rotterdam-centraal-station" class="block__title title--l">7. Rotterdam Centraal Station</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p><a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/centraal-station-rotterdam" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rotterdam Central Station </a>opened in 2014 and was designed by Team CS. The station combines glass, steel and wood in a sharp, modern design. Its angled roof canopy clearly marks the entrance to the city and reflects Rotterdam’s forward-looking character. Although the 1957 station by Sybold van Ravesteyn is no longer standing, his work can still be seen in the Rivièra Hall and many other listed buildings at <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/diergaarde-blijdorp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Diergaarde Blijdorp</a>.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-14"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Een foto van een kamer met een bank in het Marriott Hotel met uitzicht op het Rotterdam Centraal Station" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Marriott_Hotel_Rotterdam_7ec6c7ebf6.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Rotterdam Centraal Station</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-15" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="8-stadhuis-city-hall" class="block__title title--l">8. Stadhuis (City Hall)</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Completed in 1920 and designed by Henri Evers, Rotterdam City Hall is one of the few buildings on the Coolsingel that survived the bombing of 1940. Its richly detailed façade contrasts with the surrounding modern architecture. Inside, a quiet courtyard offers a moment of calm in the city centre.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-16"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="De binnentuin van het Rotterdamse Stadhuis" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Stadhuis_Rotterdam_Binnentuin_Garden_558_A6979_c02f79c4bf.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Stadhuis</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-17" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="9-stadion-feyenoord" class="block__title title--l">9. Stadion Feyenoord</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Since 1937, <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/stadion-feyenoord-de-kuip" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">De Kuip</a> has shaped the skyline of Rotterdam-Zuid. Designed by Leendert van der Vlugt of Van der Vlugt &amp; Stam, the stadium is a classic example of the Nieuwe Bouwen movement, with its focus on light, space and a clear, functional structure. The open steel construction and floating stands reflect ideas closely related to <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/guide/modernist-gems-bauhaus-in-rotterdam">Bauhaus </a>functionalism. During a stadium tour, you can visit the players’ tunnel, step onto the pitch and explore the museum, offering a rare behind-the-scenes look at this modernist landmark.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-18"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Een luchtfoto van De Kuip het voetbalstadion van Feyenoord" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Luchtfoto_De_Kuip_Feyenoord_Guido_Pijper_ac8e1b4dbb.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Stadion Feyenoord De Kuip</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="textBlock-19" class="block block--text"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__wrap ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered"><header class="block__header--indented"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 id="10-van-nellefabriek" class="block__title title--l">10. Van Nellefabriek</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><div class="block__text text--styled"><p>Designed by Brinkman and Van der Vlugt and completed in 1931, the <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/van-nelle-fabriek" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Van Nelle Factory</a> was a landmark of progressive industrial architecture. Its transparent façades, functional floor plans and use of steel and concrete make it a key example of the Nieuwe Bouwen movement. As with Bauhaus design, the focus here is on functionality, transparency and social ideals. In 2014, the complex was awarded UNESCO World Heritage status, a recognition of its global significance. The Van Nelle Factory can be visited on guided tours with <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/urbanguides" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UrbanGuides</a>, organised through the <a href="https://www.rotterdam.info/en/visit/finder-locations/chabot-museum-rotterdam" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chabot Museum</a>.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="block block--media" id="mediaBlock-20"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><div class="block__content"><figure class="media
        media--cw ls-container--s ls-gutter--desk-s ls-self-centered
        media--image"><div class="media__inner"><img loading="lazy" class="block__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 840px, 100vw" alt="Een foto van het gebouw de Van Nellefabriek in kikvorsperspectief" width="840" height="473" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Van_Nelle_Fabriek_Iris_van_den_Broek_8fc32b024f.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><figcaption class="media__meta"><span class="media__caption text--s">Van Nellefabriek</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="featuredListBlock-21" class="block block--featured-content"><div class="block--slider clickables-offset" data-cs="beige"><div class="block__inner ls-container ls-gutter ls-spacing"><header class="block__header--indented ls-gutter--desk-s"><div class="block__header-inner ls-reversed"><h2 class="block__title title--l">Discover more highlights:</h2></div></header><div class="block__content"><ul class="grid" style="--slider-offset: 0;"><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/guide/top-10-places-to-visit-in-rotterdam" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="De markt op de Binnenrotte met de Markthal door Iris van den Broek" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Markthal_Markt_Binnenrotte_Iris_van_den_Broek_528c5c170a.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Visit Rotterdam's must-sees</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 176px;">These are the top 10 places to visit in Rotterdam. The city is a hub of creativity and innovation, offering a wealth of experiences. Discover attractions that highlight the diversity of its architecture and museums, including Depot Boijmans Van Beuningen and the Markthal.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.15s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/guide/top-10-museums-and-art-institutions" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Fenix_Watertaxi_Iris_van_den_Broek_1_I0_A1526_008adf5b61.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Top Museums and Art Spaces</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 148px;">From world-famous collections to contemporary art and maritime history, Rotterdam’s museums offer something for every visitor. Discover iconic museums, cultural highlights and must-see art spaces across the city with this top 10 guide.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.3s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/guide/modernist-gems-bauhaus-in-rotterdam" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="Exterior of the Van Nelle Factory in Rotterdam, a UNESCO World Heritage Site with modernist industrial architecture." width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_van_nelle_factory_rotterdam_unesco_eae9de99a4.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">All about Bauhaus in Rotterdam</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 288px;">Bauhaus was a revolutionary school of art and design that had a lasting influence around the world, including on the architecture of Rotterdam. Its principles of simplicity and functionality can be seen in iconic buildings such as the Van Nelle Factory and Huis Sonneveld. The residential area the Kiefhoek is also an example of Bauhaus ideals in Rotterdam, closely linked to the Dutch architectural movement known as Nieuwe Bouwen.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li><li class="grid__item" style="--item-stagger: 0.44999999999999996s;"><article class="card card--slider "><a href="/en/visit/guide/top-10-attractions" class="card__link"><div class="card__inner"><div class="card__visual fit-object" aria-hidden="true"><img loading="lazy" class="card__image loading" sizes="(min-width: 1800px) 400px, (min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1024px) 45vw, 248px" alt="" width="480" height="600" srcset="" src="https://rotterdampartners-rp-website-p01.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/small_Euromast_het_Park_Iris_van_den_Broek_dbe5e51479.webp" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></div><div class="card__content"><div class="ls-reversed"><h3 class="card__title title--m">Top 10 Things to Do in Rotterdam</h3></div><div class="card__intro text--m" style="--_card-intro-height: 176px;">Discover all the must-see attractions in Rotterdam, from architectural icons to hidden gems. Take to the water with Spido or Splashtours, take in panoramic views at the Euromast or discover rare and endangered species at Diergaarde Blijdorp.</div></div></div></a><button class="card__bookmark"><div class="card__bookmark-inner"><span class="sr-text">Add to my list</span><svg class="card__bookmark-icon" width="30" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--heart"></use></svg></div></button></article></li></ul><div class="gridnav"><button class="gridnav__button gridnav__prev" disabled=""><div class="gridnav__buttoninner"><span class="sr-text">Previous</span><svg class="gridnav__icon" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--arrow-thin"></use></svg></div></button><button class="gridnav__button gridnav__next"><div class="gridnav__buttoninner"><span class="sr-text">Next</span><svg class="gridnav__icon" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><use xlink:href="#icon--arrow-thin"></use></svg></div></button></div></div></div></div></section></article></div></main><footer id="a11y-footer" class="sitefooter sf" data-cs="black"><div class="rcc-footer" data-cs="color yellow"><div class="rcc-footer__inner"><div class="rcc-footer__content"><div class="rcc-footer__wrap"><div class="rcc-footer__logo"><a href="/en/visit/rotterdam-city-card" class="rcc-footer__link"><img class="rcc-footer__logoimg" loading="lazy" width="120" height="109" alt="Rotterdam City Card" src="/images/spa/logo-rcc.svg" srcset="" data-src="" data-srcset="" data-sizes=""></a></div><div class="rcc-footer__text"><p class="rcc-footer__title title--m">Unlimited public transport &amp; 25% discount on attractions</p><div class="rcc-footer__action"><a href="